WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.933
Okay, so let's get started with today's topic,

2
00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:07.667
which is the idea of a treatment effect.

3
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:11.800
Imagine we want to know whether a training programme

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.233
actually raises people's wages.

5
00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:18.867
The naive approach is just to compare

6
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:23.033
people who took the programme with people who didn't.

7
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:27.067
But, um, those two groups might be very different

8
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:30.567
before the programme even starts.

9
00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:34.033
So today we'll look at matching,

10
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.700
which tries to compare like with like.

11
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.000
We pair each treated person

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.800
with an untreated person who looks similar

13
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.167
on the things we can observe.

14
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:52.167
Let's look at a small example on the next slide.
